<%
// locals: html (pre-rendered element markup string), bgCss (background css
// value), badgeWidth, badgeHeight. Both html/bgCss are computed by the
// route handler using public/js/name-tag-render-core.js - the exact same
// module the design editor uses to draw its live canvas, so print always
// matches design (one rendering implementation, not two hand-kept-in-sync
// copies).
//
// safeInset (optional): a real request - "name tags and schedule cards
// front and back they aren't lining up just right... give the schedule
// cards a little bit more blank border so information doesn't get cut
// off even if it's a little off." Front/back duplex alignment (see
// utils/duplexPrint.js) is already pixel-exact in software - both sides
// share the identical fixed .badge-sheet grid, with nothing about either
// side's content able to shift that grid - so residual drift is real
// physical printer/paper-feed registration error on the second pass,
// which no amount of CSS can eliminate. Rather than re-editing every
// element's saved x/y/width/height (which would only fix THIS default
// layout, not whatever an admin has already customized in the Design
// editor), scaling the whole rendered card down and letting it center
// itself in its own unchanged-size box adds real blank paper margin on
// every side regardless of the underlying template - exactly the
// fallback asked for. Only ever passed for the schedule-card side of
// admin-cards-duplex-print.ejs (the one physically flipped against its
// name tag front) - every other use of this partial (plain name tag
// prints, the side-by-side "both" printout with no physical alignment
// need, this same badge shown standalone in the Design editor/Cards
// dialog) renders full-size as before.
%>
<div class="badge-canvas" style="width:<%= badgeWidth %>px; height:<%= badgeHeight %>px; background:<%= bgCss %>;">
  <% if (typeof safeInset !== 'undefined' && safeInset) { %>
    <div class="badge-canvas-safe-inset" style="width:<%= badgeWidth %>px; height:<%= badgeHeight %>px; transform: scale(<%= safeInset %>);">
      <%- html %>
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <%- html %>
  <% } %>
</div>
